 Setup → Groups creates colored tags. Apply groups from row/header menus; click the colored description bar to adjust a line’s tags. Group totals sum tagged base costs. A line may have several groups, so adding group totals can count it twice. Groups and fringes are assigned to detail lines, not directly to accounts.
 
-### Confirm cost, inheritance and shared parent invoices
+### Details, expected cost and shared parent invoices
 
-Open **Vendor & Payments** on a detail line to choose its vendor and agreed base/fringe amounts. Confirm cost preserves the original budget and records the decision. Blank confirmed fields follow current budget values; explicit amounts remain separate from the estimate.
+Open **Vendor & Payments** on a detail line. In Details, choose a contact when known and use + to create one without losing the draft. Enter Expected base; fringes are calculated from budget settings. Confirm Expected saves the amount without changing Budgeted or posting a payment. Blank follows the budget. Confirming replaces any prior manually entered fringe override with the calculated amount.
 
 Account/sub-account six-dot menus or currency signs open parent pages. Set a default Vendor / crew member and Paid through; children inherit unless overridden. Direct payment (override parent) clears inherited payroll handling. Changing defaults does not rewrite historical payment recipients.
 
@@ -95,13 +95,13 @@ From a vendor dashboard, choose **Schedule payment** on a linked line, enter an
 
 If an existing plan covers the same obligation, use **Link existing payment plan**. A blank invoice due date preserves a linked plan’s milestone timing. Do not enter the same bill as both an unrelated invoice and an extra plan.
 
-**Schedule payment…** starts a line’s payment journey. Choose Expected or Confirmed; add an expected date and, when known, a confirmed payment date. You can leave dates and the recipient TBD at first. Red means no date, yellow expected, blue confirmed, and green paid; partially paid lines are labeled. Select **This is one of multiple payments** and add each split separately. An unsplit amount override updates the forecast without changing the original budget or Actuals. Later edit the same payment to assign a recipient; do not duplicate it. A TBD plan needs a recipient before it can be recorded as paid. On the due date or when overdue it appears at the top of Payments; selecting Paid opens an explicit confirmation, not a transfer. For simple payments, enter the final actual amount (including overtime or savings) and confirm; uncheck the settle option if the amount is only a partial payment. Actuals change only after the posting. Receipt evidence may be skipped explicitly and attached later.
+**Schedule payment…** starts a line’s payment journey. Choose Expected or Confirmed; add an expected date and, when known, a confirmed payment date. You can leave dates and the recipient TBD at first. Red means no date, yellow expected, blue confirmed, and green paid; partially paid lines are labeled. Select **This is one of multiple payments** and add each split separately. A payment amount changes the commitment forecast, not the confirmed Expected cost or Actuals. Update Expected separately in Details. Later edit the same payment to assign a recipient; do not duplicate it. A TBD plan needs a recipient before it can be recorded as paid. On the due date or when overdue it appears at the top of Payments; selecting Paid opens an explicit confirmation, not a transfer. For simple payments, enter the final actual amount (including overtime or savings) and confirm; uncheck the settle option if the amount is only a partial payment. Actuals change only after the posting. Receipt evidence may be skipped explicitly and attached later.
 
-**Add payment plan…** creates an unpaid forecast: Fixed, Percentage or Remaining balance. Unpaid percentage/balance amounts follow applicable expected costs; posted paid amounts stay fixed. Shared fixed plans split their total across lines payable to one recipient. Base and fringes may be planned together or separately. Inapplicable controls are disabled with explanations.
+**Advanced setup** in Schedule payment creates an unpaid forecast: Fixed, Percentage or Remaining balance. Unpaid percentage/balance amounts follow applicable expected costs; posted paid amounts stay fixed. Shared fixed plans split their total across lines payable to one recipient. Base and fringes may be planned together or separately. Inapplicable controls are disabled with explanations.
 
 ### Record paid, receipts and direct reimbursements
 
-Use **Record paid** for an invoice/plan. Enter the actual amount and date; partial payments allocate across remaining shares. Select/upload a receipt or payment confirmation. To proceed without it, deliberately check **Skip receipt for now**; the payment stays flagged and cannot complete line closure until evidence is attached. Attach receipt later through payment history.
+Use **Record paid** for an invoice/plan. Enter the actual amount and date; partial payments allocate across remaining shares. Select/upload a receipt or payment confirmation. To proceed without it, deliberately check **Skip receipt for now**; the payment stays flagged until evidence is attached. Attach receipt later through payment history.
 
 **Record payment without invoice…** supports Paid directly or Reimburse someone. Store the merchant/vendor separately from the reimbursement recipient, with base/fringe amounts, real paid date and optional note. This records money already paid; it does not initiate a transfer.
 
@@ -121,13 +121,11 @@ When money returns, select the original outgoing payment and relevant detail lin
 
 Use **Correct / reverse** for an erroneous posting, not a genuine refund. Original records remain. Financial postings use corrections, not Undo. Cancel an expectation if money will no longer be returned; cancellation itself posts no cash.
 
-### Expected final, Actuals, variance and closure
+### Budgeted, Expected and Actual
 
-**Budgeted** is your estimate. **Confirmed cost** is the agreement (or follows budget when blank). **Expected final** is the current forecast including paid amounts and remaining expected/committed cost. The budget column labels it EXPECTED FINAL; older releases called it Hot Cost or Est. Final.
+**Budgeted** is the original estimate. **Expected** is the confirmed cost in Details, or follows the budget when blank; received cost-reducing refunds are reflected. **Actual** is net paid, including preserved legacy opening amounts and corrections. The budget Expected column and variance use Expected.
 
-**Actuals / Net paid** are paid amounts minus received refunds and corrections, including preserved legacy opening values. Show Actuals reveals ACTUAL, VARIANCE and EXPECTED FINAL; Hide Actuals only hides those columns. Actuals cannot be typed directly. **Variance = Expected final − Budgeted**: red is over, green is under. Deposits alone do not create savings.
-
-**Finalize cost** sets remaining expected cost to zero when no further expense is due; it cannot bypass unpaid invoices. It is not the same as **Close / reopen line**, which checks outstanding money, expected refunds, receipts and legacy-value review. Reopen finalized cost/closed lines if circumstances change.
+The separate Expected final forecast keeps higher paid or scheduled commitments and warns when they exceed Expected. Confirming Expected never posts a payment, and recording Paid does not automatically change Expected. Previously closed or finalized lines retain their legacy state; reopen them explicitly from the line if needed.
 
 ### Production dates, funding and cash flow
 
